    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de946127_5a0cb340",
        "filename": "microdroid/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T15:11:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does crashdump mean? Are you talking about tombstone or something else?\n\nIf it\u0027s the tombstone, then debug policy doesn\u0027t support it for now.\n\nI think that we\u0027d better to add new debug policy node for it. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "0a0e87c0_f3e9bc0e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "6a338f5123aa07138d5b3b9d5673a5144dd1353c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee0ad2a0_b35c67b9",
        "filename": "microdroid/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T01:19:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doc isn\u0027t specifically about debug policy; the title is \u0027debugging features\u0027, so I think it\u0027s better to introduce all the debugging features we provide. gdb is also one of them. See this https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1HkvCeqwUSAJFiMkf0Ac4Dup5bepceWs_w-fe8V0whec/edit?usp\u003dsharing\n\n----\nWe don\u0027t need to have an entry in debug policy for each of the debugging features.",
      "parentUuid": "de946127_5a0cb340",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "6a338f5123aa07138d5b3b9d5673a5144dd1353c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffbf5c92_45410ea1",
        "filename": "microdroid/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-09T13:02:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should mention that only passing those DT properties to the host won\u0027t be enough and they must also be passed through pvmfw\u0027s config data. Otherwise, pvmfw will silently drop the corresponding arguments from the guest DT. We could also document this behaviour in `pvmfw/README.md` and link to that section from here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "6a338f5123aa07138d5b3b9d5673a5144dd1353c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
